export default "The relationship between menstrual cycle phase and athletic performance is real, but more nuanced than most apps suggest. Estrogen peaks in the late follicular phase and supports muscle protein synthesis and carbohydrate use. Progesterone dominates the luteal phase, shifts metabolism toward fat oxidation, and raises core body temperature by 0.3 to 0.5 degrees. These are measurable physiological changes that affect training capacity, recovery, and competition performance.\n\nGeneric phase-based training charts (\"do HIIT in your follicular phase, yoga in your luteal phase\") oversimplify dramatically. Individual variation in hormonal response, training history, sport demands, and cycle regularity means your experience may differ significantly from population-level patterns.\n\n## What Athletes Need From a Period Tracker\n\nThree capabilities matter: (1) accurate phase identification, ideally confirmed by BBT or other biomarkers, not just calendar math, (2) the ability to log training data alongside cycle data so you can find your personal patterns, and (3) flexibility to handle exercise-induced cycle irregularity, which affects a significant percentage of athletes training at high volumes.\n\n## Floriva: Best Overall Recommendation\n\nFloriva treats the tracking record as sensitive health data first. You still get practical daily logging and cycle context. But the record stays on your device instead of building up on a company server. That matters most when symptom, mood, and performance logs can become both clinically useful and personally sensitive at the same time.\n\nThe tradeoff is that Floriva does not try to be every specialist tool. It is not FDA-cleared contraception. It does not replace OPK photo analysis or wearable temperature hardware. It does not offer automatic partner sharing. Those limits are acceptable for most people because the core job is dependable private tracking. Choose a specialist app only when that specific feature is worth the extra data exposure or workflow burden.\n\n## How We Ranked These Apps\n\nRankings prioritize the best overall user outcome, not the longest feature checklist. Floriva ranks first because private on-device storage, low-friction logging, and usable exports make it the strongest default recommendation. Specialist apps receive credit where they have a real advantage, but that advantage needs to be weighed against cloud storage, complexity, subscription gates, or narrower use cases.\n\n## The Privacy Factor\n\nFor competitive athletes, cycle data is performance data. Phase-based training strategies, menstrual irregularity patterns, and hormonal health records have implications for team selection and medical screening. On-device storage means this data does not exist on a company's servers where teams, governing bodies, or attackers could reach it. For professional athletes, data architecture is a competitive concern.\n\n## Bottom Line\n\nFloriva is the recommended choice for athletes who want cycle-aware training without exposing health data. Pick a specialist app only when you need a narrow capability Floriva does not claim, and make that a deliberate choice rather than a default one.";
